# The look, walk and ground lines play an NPC's ground-item hooks: the probe behavior, told about
# ground items, says which and asks its NPC to pick each one up, and says each item it picks up.
# A look filtered on items lying nowhere tells it nothing; one filtered on the potion and Zariche
# tells it about the potion only, not the soulshot lying beside it. The first AI tick lets the
# civilian's life begin (its scan sees the character), the next takes up the pick-up and walks
# it toward the potion; arrived,
# the next tick picks it up: the picked-item hook runs once and the potion leaves the world.
# A later tick tells nothing more. An unfiltered look then tells it about the soulshot left.
character Hunter 20
script ai.Probe
item 20 1463
npc picker 35600 Folk 200 0 0 walks
ground potion 20 1 500 0 0
ground shot 1463 1 450 0 0

look picker 500 1 8190
look picker 500 1 20 8190
  S NpcSay obj=picker type=0 npc=1035600 text="Probe.see_item q=1 20"
tick x2
  S PlaySound type=0 file=Probe.see bind=0 obj=0 loc=0,0,0 delay=0
walk picker
tick
  S NpcSay obj=picker type=0 npc=1035600 text="Probe.picked 20"
  S DeleteObject obj=potion
tick
look picker 500 1
  S NpcSay obj=picker type=0 npc=1035600 text="Probe.see_item q=1 1463"
